/bin/
*.test
*.prof

# The golden corpus, and everything that reads it -- kept local, never published.
#
# testdata/molang_golden*.json is 3,120 Molang expressions taken verbatim from a
# real, private add-on. The RESULT values in it were regenerated from this
# package's own evaluator, but the expressions themselves are that project's
# authoring vocabulary and worldgen logic in plain text, so the corpus cannot
# ship. Worth knowing for whoever inherits this: grepping the corpus for a
# namespace prefix finds almost nothing. What identifies the project is the
# expressions themselves, not the identifiers in them, so the obvious check
# would have passed it.
#
# The whole set moves together because it does not decompose: bench_test.go uses
# the corpus loader too, which a search for the obvious symbol names missed --
# it was caught by moving the files aside and building, which is the check worth
# repeating if this list ever changes.
#
# A checkout without these builds, vets and passes every remaining test.
# Everything here still runs locally, unchanged:  go test ./...
/testdata/
/golden_test.go
/golden_scoped_test.go
/goldencorpus.go
/goldenscoped.go
/goldenscopes.go
/bench_test.go
/cmd/gengolden/

# Local working notes and the tooling that maintains them. Never tracked,
# never published. Nothing in the build, the tests or CI reads anything here.
#
# Back it up outside the repo: git protects none of it, and `git clean -xdf`
# would take the lot.
/research/
